        <item>
            <title>2.13.0</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 23:25:16 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>82</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.13.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[## MacroPad support

Canopy can now drive an external USB key pad ([Canopy-MacroPad](https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy-MacroPad) — currently a private repo). Each key shows one pane's activity as a colour, and pressing a key focuses that pane and brings Canopy forward — so a session waiting on you is visible, and reachable, without looking at the screen.

- **Key N is pane N**, the same meaning as Cmd+1–9. The key count comes from the device, so a wider pad needs no update here
- **Colour is state, breath is urgency.** Working and background-task keys breathe shallowly; a session waiting on your approval breathes deep, and it is the only one that does
- **Green means "finished while you weren't looking"** — including while Canopy itself was in the background. Coming back clears only the pane you returned to
- Connects automatically when the pad is plugged in, reconnects when it is unplugged, and blanks the pad when Canopy quits. Nothing changes when no pad is present
- Serial, not HID: no Input Monitoring permission, and keystrokes cannot leak into other apps

## Sidebar

The per-row activity icons (thinking flower, waiting hourglass, raised hand) are replaced by a **coloured dot** that uses the same colours, curve and timing as the pad — so a glance at the sidebar and a glance at your hand tell the same story.

Enable the pad and set LED brightness in Settings → General.
]]></description>
